🏗️ Architectural Recommendations
1. Clarify the Execution Model: Swarm vs Sequential
Your architecture documents mention both "Swarm Mode" (parallel, fast) and "Deep Mode" (sequential, autonomous). This is the right direction, but you need to implement the ExecutionMode enum in your database:

// Add to schema.prisma
enum ExecutionMode {
  SWARM     // Parallel execution (2-5 min tasks)
  DEEP      // Sequential hierarchical (1-5 hour tasks)
  HYBRID    // Starts Swarm, escalates to Deep if needed
}

model Execution {
  // ... existing fields
  mode ExecutionMode @default(SWARM)
  stateFilePath String?  // For Deep mode persistence
  retryCount Int @default(0)
  maxRetries Int @default(3)
}

Why? Users building simple content pipelines want speed. Users building Devin-style coding agents need depth. Let them choose.

2. Implement a Proper Trigger System
Currently your triggers are basic. For n8n-style automation, you need:

Trigger Type	Implementation
Webhook	✅ Have basic
Schedule (Cron)	❌ Missing
File Watch	❌ Missing
Email	❌ Missing
Database Change	❌ Missing
Manual	✅ Have
Recommendation: Create a TriggerService with a plugin architecture:

typescript
// backend/src/triggers/trigger.interface.ts
export interface Trigger {
  type: string;
  config: TriggerConfig;
  start(): Promise<void>;
  stop(): Promise<void>;
  onTrigger: (payload: any) => void;
}
// backend/src/triggers/cron.trigger.ts
@Injectable()
export class CronTrigger implements Trigger {
  private job: CronJob;
  
  async start() {
    this.job = new CronJob(this.config.schedule, () => {
      this.onTrigger({ triggeredAt: new Date(), type: 'cron' });
    });
    this.job.start();
  }
}
