4. Agent Configuration: Make it Customizable Without Code
Your Agent model has the right fields, but users can't configure them from the UI. Create a Node Inspector Panel that shows when a node is selected:

tsx
// frontend/components/NodeInspector.tsx
interface NodeInspectorProps {
  selectedNode: Node | null;
  onUpdate: (nodeId: string, data: any) => void;
}
const NodeInspector = ({ selectedNode, onUpdate }: NodeInspectorProps) => {
  if (!selectedNode) return <EmptyState />;
  
  switch (selectedNode.type) {
    case 'agent':
      return <AgentInspector node={selectedNode} onUpdate={onUpdate} />;
    case 'trigger':
      return <TriggerInspector node={selectedNode} onUpdate={onUpdate} />;
    // ... other node types
  }
};
Agent Inspector Fields:

Model selection (dropdown with GPT-4, Claude, Gemini, etc.)
Temperature slider (0-2)
Max tokens input
System prompt editor (with syntax highlighting)
Tools enabled (checkbox list)
Memory type (none, conversation, vector)
5. Safety & Guardrails: Production-Critical
Your safety_tickets table is a good start, but you need proactive safety, not just reactive:

Safety Architecture
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Safety Middleware Layer                      │
├───────────────────────┬───────────────────┬────────────────────┤
│   Input Validation    │  Output Guardrails │  Budget Controls   │
│                       │                    │                    │
│ • Prompt injection    │ • PII detection    │ • Per-execution $  │
│ • Size limits         │ • Toxic content    │ • Daily limit      │
│ • Schema validation   │ • Hallucination    │ • Per-user limit   │
│                       │   detection        │ • Emergency stop   │
└───────────────────────┴───────────────────┴────────────────────┘
Add to every LLM call:

python
# python_engine/safety.py
class SafetyGuard:
    def __init__(self, budget_usd: float = 10.0):
        self.budget = budget_usd
        self.spent = 0.0
    
    def pre_check(self, prompt: str) -> Tuple[bool, str]:
        """Run before LLM call"""
        if len(prompt) > 50000:
            return False, "Prompt too long"
        if self.detect_prompt_injection(prompt):
            return False, "Potential prompt injection detected"
        if self.spent >= self.budget:
            return False, "Budget exhausted"
        return True, "OK"
    
    def post_check(self, response: str) -> Tuple[bool, str]:
        """Run after LLM call"""
        if self.detect_pii(response):
            return False, "PII detected in output"
        return True, "OK"
    
    def detect_prompt_injection(self, text: str) -> bool:
        patterns = [
            r"ignore previous instructions",
            r"disregard all",
            r"you are now",
            r"new task:",
        ]
        return any(re.search(p, text.lower()) for p in patterns)
