Summary
Your platform has strong bones — solid tech stack (NestJS + React + Python), well-designed data models, and the hybrid Swarm/Deep execution concept is innovative.

The gaps are in UX and production-readiness, not architecture. Focus on:

Making it usable without code (Node library, inspector)
Making it safe (budgets, guardrails, approvals)
Making it observable (cost analytics, logging)
Would you like me to start implementing any of these recommendations? I'd suggest starting with the Node Library Panel — it's high-impact and will immediately make the platform feel more like n8n.




